The attached image is a box plot illustrating the anti-rPA IgG titers in mice immunized with recombinant protective antigen (rPA) alone or formulated with various doses of aluminum hydroxide (AH) or Nano-11. The data shows that Nano-11 significantly enhances the antibody response, with all tested concentrations (12.5, 50, and 200 µg/dose) yielding significantly higher IgG titers compared to rPA alone. Notably, even the lowest dose of Nano-11 (12.5 µg) induces a strong antibody response, unlike AH which is ineffective at this concentration, supporting Nano-11's efficacy as a potent vaccine adjuvant.